        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs: history APIs silently no-op on rate limiting per spec]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45132</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45132"/>
        <updated>2026-08-14T08:21:23.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #44477.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4667059019" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44477" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/44477/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44477">#44477</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The History API pages claimed that <code class="notranslate">pushState()</code>, <code class="notranslate">replaceState()</code>, <code class="notranslate">back()</code>, <code class="notranslate">go()</code>, and <code class="notranslate">forward()</code> throw a <code class="notranslate">SecurityError</code> when called too frequently. Per <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4531528389" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12492" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/pull/12492/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12492">whatwg/html#12492</a> (merged 2026-06-16), the spec changed: the navigable's "allowed to perform a navigation or history update" algorithm now returns <code class="notranslate">blocked</code> when the API is invoked too frequently, and the method silently returns instead of throwing.</p>
<p dir="auto">I checked the current HTML spec before making this change: the shared history push/replace state steps and the delta traverse steps both consult the navigable's allowed-to-perform check and return on <code class="notranslate">blocked</code>. The remaining <code class="notranslate">SecurityError</code> cases (document not fully active, invalid/cross-origin URL) are unchanged.</p>
<p dir="auto">Changes (5 pages):</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">History/pushState</code> and <code class="notranslate">History/replaceState</code>: removed "or if the method is called too frequently" from the <code class="notranslate">SecurityError</code> description; added a note that rate-limited calls are silently ignored, with the rate limit being implementation-defined.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">History/back</code>, <code class="notranslate">History/go</code>, <code class="notranslate">History/forward</code>: removed the sentence about throwing/warning/ignoring on throttling; added the same note.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">The pages described behavior that no longer matches the spec or current Chromium behavior, which misled developers who relied on catching a <code class="notranslate">SecurityError</code> to detect rate limiting.</p>]]></content>
