        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs: use generic() syntax for script-specific font families]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45124</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45124"/>
        <updated>2026-08-14T08:21:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43412.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4063297756" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43412/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412">#43412</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">font-family</code> page listed <code class="notranslate">fangsong</code> as a plain generic-family keyword, but per the CSS Fonts 4 spec the script-specific generic font families use the functional <code class="notranslate">generic()</code> syntax: <code class="notranslate">generic(fangsong)</code>, <code class="notranslate">generic(kai)</code>, <code class="notranslate">generic(khmer-mul)</code>, <code class="notranslate">generic(nastaliq)</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Changes:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Syntax section: <code class="notranslate">font-family: fangsong;</code> → <code class="notranslate">font-family: generic(fangsong);</code>.</li>
<li>Values section: replaced the bare <code class="notranslate">fangsong</code> bullet with the four script-specific <code class="notranslate">generic()</code> families, described per the spec, with a note that they are not yet supported by any browser.</li>
<li>Examples: removed the fangsong live-example block, since no browser supports the value.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">The page previously suggested <code class="notranslate">fangsong</code> was a usable keyword value, which is not the case: the bare keyword is not in the current spec grammar, and no browser supports these values.</p>]]></content>
